From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:13:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wpt: Add the QuickJS expectations

The results of `--js-engine quickjs` that differ from SpiderMonkey's,
as `js_engine` conditions in 91 expectation files:

- WebAssembly, which QuickJS doesn't have: wasm/,
  content-security-policy/wasm-unsafe-eval and WebGL conformance2/wasm
  are disabled for QuickJS. Tests elsewhere that need it get
  expectations, e.g. the origin-keyed-agent-clusters tests, which detect
  agent clusters by posting a WebAssembly.Module.
- QuickJS gaps, e.g. `Intl` (missing in the desktop build only), the
  eval column in CSP reports, error stacks in structured clones, and
  WebGL timeouts from interpreter speed.
- Tests QuickJS passes where SpiderMonkey hits a Servo bug, e.g. module
  errors with top-level await in the bfcache and import-map tests.

Fork note: regenerated at each sync (docs/ohos-sync.md, step 3.8); the
runbook steps are in this commit.

Drop the QuickJS conditions of the media tests that failed because
nothing kept unreferenced media elements alive: autoplay.html,
allowed-to-play.html, resource-selection-candidate-moved.html and the
autoplay-allowed-by and autoplay-default permissions policy tests. Patch 69
fixes that, and QuickJS gives SpiderMonkey's results for them now.
Patch 69 drops the conditions of autoplay-disabled-by-permissions-policy
itself, because it edits that file after this one.

Validation: a full local WPT run of the QuickJS build (servo-quickjs 72fa2b6, 58,101 tests) had 162 tests with unexpected results; those were rerun 3 times with each engine, and only results that never occurred with SpiderMonkey were kept (443 results in 94 tests; 89 that varied or occurred with both engines were left to the SpiderMonkey expectations). Every changed file evaluates the same for SpiderMonkey as before. Rerunning the 162 tests against the new expectations, QuickJS had 45 tests with unexpected results and SpiderMonkey 46, nearly all the same host effects; the 6 with QuickJS only are among the results that varied between runs. 2026-10-13 sync: a full QuickJS run of the rebased stack (servo-quickjs cbf02ee, 58,340 tests) had 76 tests with unexpected results; after 3 reruns with each engine, the 7 whose results recurred in every QuickJS run and never occurred with SpiderMonkey were updated (six media tests of the media-element lifetime gap and sandbox-window-open-srcdoc), and then ran as expected with QuickJS. Media tests that no longer lose their elements: QuickJS release build of this branch, `./mach test-wpt --js-engine quickjs --processes 2` of these tests, autoplay-disabled-by-permissions-policy, played-loop and the new gc-unreferenced-media-element.html, 2 runs: all as expected for SpiderMonkey, apart from autoplay-default-permissions-policy, which is OK on this host with either engine against its TIMEOUT expectation; without patches 68 to 70 the QuickJS build times out in these tests as the dropped conditions expected.
